  "description": "UPEMUA crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C126 H112 Dy10 N30 O44,C1 H4 O1,8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5A (Dy) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.714-3.937 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.46-114.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy10(L2)4(μ2-OH)2(μ3-OH)4(NO3)4(CH3CN)2(CH3OH)4(H2O)8]·CH3OH·8H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
